<title>BELGIUM: Cockerill plunges into 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Cockerill plunges into 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss (ex-minorities)	9.00 vs    3.2 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - Cockerill Sambre Group is Belgium's largest steel maker. The group said that the nine billion franc loss included 7.7 billion francs worth of exceptional charges. The charges are partly related to Cockerill's &quot;Horizon 2000&quot; restructuring plan.  </p>
<p>    Cons turnover			   203.14 vs   206.66</p>
<p>    Operating profit			  0.63 vs     8.95</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss			  7.70 vs     2.09</p>
<p>    Net financial debt		     20.97 vs    20.98</p>
<p>    Crude steel production   6.35 million tonnes vs 6.33 million</p>
<p>Note - Cockerill said in a statement that steel prices had fallen throughout 1996 and the first quarter of 1997 started with very low prices.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
